{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 121, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-to-output residual where none existed gives a much larger gain than swapping it in for an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting the residual shortcut hurts trainability far more than deleting a conv or pool on edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty node2-to-output edge opens a new deep path, which beats replacing an op that already carries signal."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 0 is none, node 1 is dead, so the edit also activates edges 2 and 4 and gives a large gain."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where the node1-to-node2 link is missing increases depth and capacity more than replacing an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on an empty input-to-node2 edge adds a new feature path, a larger benefit than an op swap."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 empty, edge 4 is the only deep path to the output, so removing it is much more damaging."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 empty, edge 5 is the only deep path to the output, so removing it collapses the cell toward a shallow network."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without a direct input-to-output skip, a skip on e